From 0517a65cc1b98f30aac1b95110df771c8b8e338e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:21:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 242/280] WIP: drm/rockchip: dw_hdmi_qp: attach the Broadcast
 RGB property

The HDMI connector state helper already derives is_limited_range and the
AVI InfoFrame quantization range from the Broadcast RGB setting, but the
property was never attached to the dw-hdmi-qp bridge connector. Userspace
therefore could not select full range, and every CTA mode was limited
range.

Standard Dolby Vision requires full-range RGB, so attach the property
after creating the bridge connector. The default remains Automatic so
existing behaviour is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
index aeba16ffa80c..f268d3620b0c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
@@ -760,6 +760,11 @@ static int dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_bind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(connector),
 				     "Failed to init bridge connector\n");
 
+	ret = drm_connector_attach_broadcast_rgb_property(connector);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+				     "Failed to attach Broadcast RGB property\n");
+
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, hdmi);
 
 	return 0;
